ana: heads-up: found a docs/regression where our SDK snippets for streaming+paginators assume whole-page retries. gateway now emits resume tokens so clients can resume mid-page. we need quick updates for py/ts/go examples and a short note in Streaming guide.
marie: thanks. i saw flaky e2e too. i'll take TS. will add an async-iterator example showing how to capture and call resume(token).
dan: i'll handle Go. prefer explicit ResumeToken field in request and show exponential backoff with jitter.
eli: i'll do Python and write the blurb about server truncation semantics + recommended backoff defaults. also add a short RELEASE_NOTES entry.
nana: small TS draft from marie (please adapt to published SDK surface):
```ts
// resumable stream+paginator (SDK-style pseudo)
const it = client.streamPaginate('/v1/resumable')
for await (const page of it) {
  for (const chunk of page.chunks) process.stdout.write(chunk.text)
  const tok = page.headers['x-resume-token']
  if (tok) it.resume(tok)
}
```
marie: i'll include detection of truncation (502 + header) and a helper retry wrapper.
dan: Go pseudo snippet:
```go
req := &client.PaginateRequest{Path: "/v1/resumable"}
back := NewBackoff(200*time.Millisecond, 3*time.Second, true)
for {
  resp, err := client.StreamPaginate(ctx, req)
  if err != nil {
    time.Sleep(back.Next())
    continue
  }
  io.Copy(os.Stdout, resp.Body)
  tok := resp.Header.Get("X-Resume-Token")
  if tok == "" { break }
  req.ResumeToken = tok
}
```
eli: Python pseudo: small helper to track resume_token and jittered sleeps:
```python
client = RedwoodClient()
resume = None
while True:
    resp = client.stream_paginate('/v1/resumable', resume_token=resume)
    for p in resp.pages():
        for c in p.chunks: print(c.text, end='')
    resume = resp.headers.get('x-resume-token')
    if not resume: break
    sleep(jittered_backoff())
```
nana: docs blurb suggestion: "Servers may truncate long streaming responses under load. When responses include X-Resume-Token, clients should attempt bounded retries using that token to resume within the same logical page. Avoid re-fetching the entire page; prefer server-provided resume tokens and an idempotent cursor. Recommended backoff: base=200ms, max=3s, attempts=5, jitter=true."
marie: i'll add TS unit-ish example and a tiny link to RELEASE_NOTES.
dan: i'll add a basic lint in docs-ci to search code blocks for 'x-resume-token' to avoid regressions.
